#N Max (spacefiller)
#O Tim Coe, 1995
#C The smallest known spacefiller: its edges race outwards at c/2 and leave
#C behind a periodic agar of density 1/2, so the population grows
#C quadratically.
#C Verified by the Emergence Lab verifier (B3/S23, unbounded grid):
#C quadratic growth; populations gen 200: 12095, gen 400: 43995, gen 600:
#C 95895, gen 800: 167795; equal-step second differences 20000 and 20000.
#C Source: Life Lexicon Release 29, entry "spacefiller", diagram 1 (bundled
#C with Golly 5.1 at Help/Lexicon/).
